[{:db/id "q-15457/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "6ce6b55c-f51e-5a76-9782-ae5e346fb42e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15457/selection/6c5db99f36b63a9fa5a4a0d244481e2d27c082d81f40dba553a9e968f6ecc732" :answer/id #uuid "b29d8346-6d37-530f-8757-381236111818" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15457/selection/f6f0a48b5e70bee7bf866845de273c53adf523517f98dc895c981759ddf58c84" :answer/id #uuid "1324b2b8-e238-5bff-8f34-2b102dd2d6eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15457/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "517d6982-f305-577e-87cc-be4e0e966542" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15457/selection/df62a440927177d32f71c7e130b02360d8e2f7292a3956a8d6a8fca21c97f3f8" :answer/id #uuid "0d60e1b7-d80e-5ec8-b197-8f8e3e7976c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15457/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc35beed-7ff2-518c-977d-441db5683bef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15457/selection/f6f0a48b5e70bee7bf866845de273c53adf523517f98dc895c981759ddf58c84" :answer-field/choices ["q-15457/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-15457/selection/6c5db99f36b63a9fa5a4a0d244481e2d27c082d81f40dba553a9e968f6ecc732" "q-15457/selection/f6f0a48b5e70bee7bf866845de273c53adf523517f98dc895c981759ddf58c84" "q-15457/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-15457/selection/df62a440927177d32f71c7e130b02360d8e2f7292a3956a8d6a8fca21c97f3f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15457" :question/id #uuid "a30e060e-8fbc-5c7c-b8b0-45023960607a" :question/math-academy-id "q-15457" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,y={cos}^{2}⁡(t),\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-15457/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15457"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-15469/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "e7392b79-be64-50f2-83be-35fc7f0a24bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15469/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "916b006c-543c-5c12-9315-ed7021903064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15469/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "73ac7292-924c-5976-9a55-cb32e87c3d3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15469/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "7b7b6f22-1628-5746-aeff-15d4bf0f2d84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15469/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "57a0dad2-5f05-5730-82a8-3433df852bf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15469/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5a81521-a24f-5dd0-87f2-f8493118e35e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15469/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer-field/choices ["q-15469/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-15469/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-15469/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-15469/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-15469/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15469" :question/id #uuid "7f9e0331-ffe6-5489-b436-faf1f0bea590" :question/math-academy-id "q-15469" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{3}+1,\\,y={t}^{4}+2{t}^{2},\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6{t}^{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=4t({t}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{4t({t}^{2}+1)}{6{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({t}^{2}+1)}{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2((1)^{2}+1)}{3\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-15469/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15469"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102940/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "580202dd-3fea-5679-af87-c2bc9c132183" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102940/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "53825d27-7c1f-5288-b7f6-b208c4a85b1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102940/selection/fba918d936ec8a8857b6fc6984940ee860d3d39fbe77c995f1d64ac962ebb2cd" :answer/id #uuid "8f9373b0-73fa-5a8e-8ec4-b45683795d8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102940/selection/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" :answer/id #uuid "92d654cf-26ee-54fa-9c1e-ef823f34bec3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102940/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" :answer/id #uuid "e7c57dc7-1f1a-5a6e-b1a2-16b6f0e563df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102940/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4ab19c6-acbb-5c20-a748-33e4d8506737" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102940/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-102940/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" "q-102940/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-102940/selection/fba918d936ec8a8857b6fc6984940ee860d3d39fbe77c995f1d64ac962ebb2cd" "q-102940/selection/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" "q-102940/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102940" :question/id #uuid "7624a235-ab14-553b-803a-f56f725749db" :question/math-academy-id "q-102940" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{2}+3,\\,y=3{t}^{5}+{t}^{3},\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}(5{t}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3{t}^{2}(5{t}^{2}+1)}{4t}=\\frac{3t(5{t}^{2}+1)}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3(1)(5(1)^{2}+1)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102940/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102940"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353340/field-1/74b9878323186062e434675fc3ee407e9e4a746d2cc85ca785d4664ca99bda01" :answer/id #uuid "5e3ed63d-fc55-5d63-857c-b186e66f8b7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353340/field-1/2a28a53216361474017108aa9cf0fffd0fb392524d53aeb00b78355e4fa703c6" :answer/id #uuid "499b0218-ae69-579d-9205-ae2ed67fa112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353340/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "13484f49-5055-5f6f-abda-84c97c7d98f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353340/field-1/74b9878323186062e434675fc3ee407e9e4a746d2cc85ca785d4664ca99bda01" :answer-field/choices ["q-353340/field-1/74b9878323186062e434675fc3ee407e9e4a746d2cc85ca785d4664ca99bda01" "q-353340/field-1/2a28a53216361474017108aa9cf0fffd0fb392524d53aeb00b78355e4fa703c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353340" :question/id #uuid "bcc9886b-9868-59ad-af40-79950852f43a" :question/math-academy-id "q-353340" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979831/assets/e0b1dc90950ba127e90fce400bc7ed1b6e8dd8e710ff880ab5949521b02a258a.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=4{e}^{-t},\\,y={t}^{2}+6t,\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,1}=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-4{e}^{-t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t+6.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2t+6}{(-4{e}^{-t})}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,1} & =\\frac{2(1)+6}{(-4{e}^{-1})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8e}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353340/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353340"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353347/field-1/f739025c4f94ed1c280420826f05664d3778e2035846ef60903b143e289aaeaf" :answer/id #uuid "c1b35709-7ba5-5d24-a5b7-0c00dd296e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}e^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353347/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5333d5a-78d9-5430-ba42-aef3ddd114ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353347/field-1/f739025c4f94ed1c280420826f05664d3778e2035846ef60903b143e289aaeaf" :answer-field/choices ["q-353347/field-1/f739025c4f94ed1c280420826f05664d3778e2035846ef60903b143e289aaeaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353347" :question/id #uuid "cee6bcbe-4838-5f33-9194-61f49470e510" :question/math-academy-id "q-353347" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{3t},\\,y=2{e}^{t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ as a function of $t.$\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{3{e}^{3t}}=\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-2t}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353347/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
